CRITICAL — chapter narrative timeline (for the catalog / UI):
When finishing a chapter snapshot, also prepare (or update) narrative chronology metadata for that chapter so the app can show story-time, ages, and a scrubber. Prefer adding a `narrative` object on the chapter entry in `public/ged/catalog.json`:
```
"narrative": {
  "start": "1314-03-15T14:00:00",
  "end": "1314-03-15T18:00:00",
  "spanLabel": "Un après-midi (quelques heures)",
  "location": "Château de Westminster, Angleterre",
  "note": "Optional caveat when the exact day/hour is inferred.",
  "sourceQuote": "Verbatim book phrase that anchors the dating.",
  "moments": [
    { "at": "1314-03-15T14:00:00", "label": "…", "summary": "…" }
  ]
}
```
`start` / `end` = narrative clock for the span covered by this snapshot (not publication time). `spanLabel` = human duration of story-time between start and end. `moments` = key dated beats the scrubber can snap to. Do not invent dates that contradict the text; if only “mars 1314” / “un après-midi” is known, say so in `note` and use a conventional day only as a frieze anchor.

